{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of your neurology team doctors. You’re here today for your 10th cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your brain lymphoma, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been feeling okay since my last treatment. No new symptoms or anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. We’ll be giving the chemotherapy today around noon. We’ll monitor you closely, as we know nausea and joint aches can happen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. The nausea was rough, but the medicine helped. Is it normal to feel achy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s a common side effect. We’ll give you ondansetron and ativan if needed. Your labs this morning look stable, so we’re good to proceed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. And my blood clot medicine—enoxaparin—I’m still on that, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll continue that twice daily. It’s important to prevent another clot, especially with your history of DVT and PE."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my asthma? I’ve been using my inhaler like usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Your lungs sounded clear this morning. We’ll keep you on your fluticasone-salmeterol and montelukast. We did notice your eosinophils are a bit high, but that’s likely related to your asthma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-09-08 08:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not in this case. It’s mild and expected with asthma. We’re not concerned, especially since you’re already on treatment for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-09-08 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You just finished the methotrexate infusion. Everything went smoothly. Any nausea or discomfort so far?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-09-08 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little queasy, actually. And my shoulders feel stiff."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-09-08 12:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you some ondansetron for the nausea and monitor the aches. The stiffness should ease in a day or so."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-09-08 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. Will I be able to go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-09-08 12:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not quite. We need to check your methotrexate level at 24 and 48 hours. We can’t discharge you until it drops low enough to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-09-08 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right. I forgot about that. So probably in a few days?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-09-08 12:24:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely Thursday or Friday. We’ll keep you updated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-09-09 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your 24-hour methotrexate level came back at 1.0, which is expected. It’s starting to clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-09-09 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a good number?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-09-09 07:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s where we expect it to be at this stage. We’ll check again tomorrow. If it drops below 0.1, you can go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-09-09 07:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my liver? Last time my enzymes went up a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-09-09 07:36:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re watching that. Your ALT and AST were normal before chemo, but they often rise a bit afterward. We’ll check them again today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-09-09 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my colitis? I haven’t had any bowel issues, but I stopped mesalamine again before coming in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-09-09 07:39:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can restart it when you go home. We’ll make sure it’s on your discharge list."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-09-09 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick update—your liver enzymes are up, as expected. ALT is 134 and AST is 86. But they’re already starting to come down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-09-09 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-09-09 14:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not really. It’s a known side effect of methotrexate and usually resolves on its own. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your methotrexate level dropped to 0.09 this morning. That’s low enough for safe discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, once we finalize your discharge paperwork. Your liver numbers are improving, and you’re feeling better overall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my next chemo? When is that scheduled?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In about four weeks. You’ll also have an MRI before that to check how the tumor is responding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time the MRI showed the lesion was shrinking. I’m hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a very positive sign. We’re encouraged by your progress so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my foot pain? It’s still there, but gabapentin helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep you on gabapentin for that. It’s chronic, but we’re managing it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I keep taking the enoxaparin at home, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, twice daily. Don’t stop unless we tell you. It’s important for preventing clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my seizure medicine—levetiracetam—I should keep that up too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s part of your routine now. We haven’t seen any seizures, so that’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no more steroids this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not this cycle. We’re trying to minimize them unless needed. Your neurologic exam remains stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I had trouble sleeping when I was on them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-09-10 08:24:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep that in mind for future cycles. For now, you’re doing well without them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-09-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. We’re finalizing your discharge. You’re cleared to go home in about an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-09-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any final instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-09-11 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your home meds except mesalamine—we’ll restart that today. Drink plenty of fluids, watch for fever or unusual pain, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-09-11 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll see oncology in four weeks?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-09-11 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and the MRI is scheduled for the week before. We’ll send you the details."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2175-09-11 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2175-09-11 09:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did great this cycle. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2175-09-11 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2175-09-11 10:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. No nausea, no aches. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2175-09-11 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Your vitals are stable, and your exam is unchanged. We’re discharging you in good condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2175-09-11 10:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood work? Is everything back to normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2175-09-11 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your methotrexate is cleared, and your liver enzymes are improving. Blood counts are a bit low but expected after chemo. They’ll recover."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2175-09-11 10:37:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2175-09-11 10:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Take care, and we’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2175-09-11 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I avoid crowds or sick people?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2175-09-11 11:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, good question. Your white count is a bit low, so try to avoid sick contacts and wash your hands often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2175-09-11 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And if I get a fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2175-09-11 11:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us right away. Fever over 100.4 could be serious. Don’t wait."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2175-09-11 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2175-09-11 11:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2175-09-11 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just wanted to say I feel really supported. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2175-09-11 11:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here for you. Keep fighting—you’re doing well."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2175-09-08 00:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2175-09-11 13:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, ulcerative colitis, asthma, and a history of DVT/PE was admitted for her 10th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the treatment well, with mild transaminitis and manageable nausea and arthralgias that resolved within 24 hours. Methotrexate levels decreased appropriately by day three, allowing for safe discharge. She remained neurologically stable throughout the admission, with chronic right foot pain controlled on gabapentin. Her eosinophilia was noted but attributed to asthma and managed with montelukast. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to restart mesalamine, continue enoxaparin, and follow up with oncology in four weeks for her next cycle and MRI.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Ulcerative colitis, unspecified",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Multiple sclerosis",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Other chronic pain"
    ]
  }
}
